# Profile "local": Elasticsearch + Kibana running on this Mac (e.g. Kibana's `yarn es snapshot`).
# Copy to .env.edot.local (gitignored), then: ./scripts/install-edot.sh local
#
# In Kibana (http://localhost:5601/.../app/observabilityOnboarding/kubernetes) the
# onboarding page prints these three values in its kubectl/helm snippet.
# localhost is rewritten to host.docker.internal automatically (pods can't see the Mac's localhost).
ELASTIC_ENDPOINT='http://localhost:9200'
ELASTIC_API_KEY='<elastic_api_key from the onboarding page>'
ONBOARDING_ID='<onboarding.id value from the onboarding page>'
